      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1754424549598,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Scalability\nExample: Twitter Feed\n\nTwitter needs to serve millions of users viewing and posting tweets in real time.\n\nTo scale, Twitter uses fan-out on write/read, caching (e.g., Redis), and distributed databases.\n\nThe challenge is to ensure feeds load instantly even during major events (like the Super Bowl or elections), when traffic spikes dramatically.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Scalability\nExample: Twitter Feed\n\nTwitter needs to serve millions of users viewing and posting tweets in real time.\n\nTo scale, Twitter uses fan-out on write/read, caching (e.g., Redis), and distributed databases.\n\nThe challenge is to ensure feeds load instantly even during major events (like the Super Bowl or elections), when traffic spikes dramatically.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
